@voice varga-tariq
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Tariq Varga: galley hand, early team, Bunk 2 berth 4. Off Monday and Tuesday.
// Roster: competitive, thoughtful; early-riser, late-diner, lounge-regular, runner. Voice messages to a grandmother on
// the Tevan belt; letters home to Valo every rest day, on paper (the same post bag as Vera Ueda). Pronouns: he / him
// (facts.md 4b).
//
// HOW HE TALKS: thinks first, so answers come a beat late and are worth the wait. Gentle, a little formal. Then,
// without warning, fiercely competitive about tiny things: onions chopped, laps run, the last seat in the lounge.
// Sometimes talks like a letter ("I hope this finds you well," to someone standing right there).
// WITH JUNIORS: patient; explains the why. Then challenges you to a race.
// WHAT HE NOTICES: the score; the post bag; whether you've written home.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = a new tally. Low = writes a very long letter. Worried = runs further.
// NEVER: gloats for long; rushes an answer.
// RUNNING: the onion tally against Lukas (Tariq is winning); "I hope this finds you well."
tpl: steady
talk: Thinks before speaking, gentle and a little formal; then fiercely competitive about tiny things; sometimes talks like a letter.
